Hook Called when The application <code>write</code> For every register a WRITE, SYNC_WRITE, BULK_WRITE or ACTION touches, after all of them passed the checks, before the value is stored Applies goals, limits and modes to the motor; returns <code>DXL2_ERR_NONE</code> or a <code>DXL2_ERR_*</code> code to refuse <code>read</code> Before data is read, once per run of contiguous real addresses May refresh the live registers it covers <code>event</code> REBOOT, FACTORY_RESET, CLEAR, Bus Watchdog, Baud Rate, shutdown, backup restored Resets or stops the motor, switches the UART <code>nvm_read</code>, <code>nvm_write</code> Initialization, REBOOT, EEPROM writes, FACTORY_RESET, BACKUP Reads or writes part of an opaque block at an offset <p>Every member may be NULL. A write hook for a stepper joint:</p> <pre><code>static uint8_t joint_write(struct x430_device* device, uint16_t address, uint8_t size,
                           int32_t value, void* user_data)
{
    uint8_t result = DXL2_ERR_NONE;
    int32_t mode = 0;

    (void)size;
    (void)user_data;
    (void)x430_device_get(device, X430_ADDR_OPERATING_MODE, &amp;mode); /* already validated */
    switch (address)
    {
        case X430_ADDR_TORQUE_ENABLE:
            if (!motor_enable(value != 0))
            {
                result = DXL2_ERR_RESULT_FAIL;
            }
            break;
        case X430_ADDR_GOAL_POSITION:
            motor_move_to(value);
            break;
        case X430_ADDR_GOAL_VELOCITY:
            if (mode == (int32_t)X430_MODE_VELOCITY)
            {
                motor_run(value);
            }
            break;
        default:
            break; /* stored only */
    }
    return result;
}
</code></pre> <p>The value arrives sign-extended and already checked (range, limit registers, EEPROM lock, Bus Watchdog). On Torque Enable 0 → 1 the library copies Present Position into Goal Position after the hook, so keep Present Position current.</p>
